   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Hi All,</span><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;vertical-align:baseline;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><br></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;vertical-align:baseline;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">I need help with Subset.</div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;vertical-align:baseline;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">I&#39;m having issues using the Deducer Data Subset tool, and the Deducer wiki entry for Subset is a placeholder only with no information. Basically, I would like to generate a subset of data to exclude entries based on batching two variables per evaluation, I&#39;ve attached a simple .robj dataset as a simple example.</div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;vertical-align:baseline;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><br></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;vertical-align:baseline;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">There are two dataset variables, Sample, and Age that are of importance.</div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;vertical-align:baseline;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><br></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;vertical-align:baseline;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">If I do:</div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;vertical-align:baseline;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">====</div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;vertical-align:baseline;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Sample != (&quot;L1_F1L&quot;) &amp; Sample != (&quot;L1_F1R&quot;) &amp; Sample != (&quot;L1_F2L&quot;)</div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;vertical-align:baseline;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">====</div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;vertical-align:baseline;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">I generate a subset that has samples L1_F1L, L1_F1R and L1_F2L removed. </div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;vertical-align:baseline;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">In my case, this causes issues because there are multiple rows with the same &quot;Sample&quot; string. I only want to exclude those of Age == &quot;E16.5&quot; not &quot;E19.5&quot;.</div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;vertical-align:baseline;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><br></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;vertical-align:baseline;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">So, I&#39;d like to nest the subset, so it removes Samples L1_F1L, L1_F1R and L1_F2L IF they are &#39;Age == &quot;E16.5&quot; &#39; but not if they are &quot;E19.5&quot;.</div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;vertical-align:baseline;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><br></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;vertical-align:baseline;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">I don&#39;t know how to frame the logical expression to evaluate two conditions per row.</div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;vertical-align:baseline;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><br></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;vertical-align:baseline;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">best regards,</div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;vertical-align:baseline;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Kieran</div></div>\r\n"
    ]
   ]
  },
